# Data warehouse migration & re-architecture {#top}

## Executive summary {#summary}

We are moving the analytics warehouse off the legacy cluster onto the new
columnar store. This document is the plan of record: scope, phasing, cost,
and the rollback position at each gate. It is revised weekly and is edited
by both the platform team and an agent that keeps the cost tables in step
with the latest capacity numbers.

## Scope {#scope}

In scope: the fact tables, the nightly ELT jobs, the semantic layer, and the
downstream BI extracts. Out of scope: the streaming ingest path, which stays
on the existing broker until the migration is signed off.

## Migration plan {#migration-plan}

Three phases, each with an explicit exit gate. No phase begins before the
previous gate is signed off by both platform-eng and the data consumers.

Phase 1 shadows the new store behind the existing one and compares results.
Phase 2 cuts the nightly ELT over and keeps the legacy path warm. Phase 3
retires the legacy cluster and reclaims its capacity.

