## Risk register {#risks}

The dominant risk is silent divergence between the two stores during the
shadow period. Mitigation is a row-level checksum job that runs after every
nightly load and fails loudly rather than logging a warning.

Secondary risks: BI extract schema drift, and the cost of running both
clusters in parallel for the length of phase 2. See [[#capacity]] for the
parallel-run cost.

## Rollback position {#rollback}

At every gate the legacy cluster is still authoritative and can be restored
by pointing the semantic layer back at it. The point of no return is the
phase 3 capacity reclaim, which is deliberately the last step.

## Open questions {#open-questions}

RESOLVED 2026-07-25: the semantic layer migrates in phase 2. Budget impact
of the shortened parallel-run window is reflected in [[#capacity]].

